# API realtime

For mutations that affect an open surface or another device/user, update the
relevant subscribed clients. A deliberate fetch-on-open surface can stay bounded
by its product scope; this rule does not require expanding the feature.

- Feature services use typed methods on `PresenceRealtimeService`, not Socket.IO
  directly. Its per-user/room emits publish to Redis even without a local server,
  allowing `RUN_HTTP=false` workers to reach clients. Pub/sub is not an outbox.
- Committed content updates stay on the request path; notification/badge emits
  accompany their worker-owned writes. See [side effects](65-async-side-effects.mdc).
- Authorize every recipient. Room payloads must not contain viewer-private fields;
  use per-user methods when audiences need different data.
- Reuse existing event names exactly; the current protocol includes legacy casing.
  Notify both sides of entity lifecycle changes, including responses to invites.
- Follow [payload/merge policy](../../docs/engineering-policy.md#realtime-contracts-and-ownership)
  for snapshots, patches, removals, and invalidations. Do not reset notification
  read/delivery state as a general realtime rule; use the owning writer's semantics.

Pointers: `src/modules/presence/presence-realtime.service.ts`,
`src/common/dto/realtime.dto.ts` (including `WsEventNames`).
Cover affected emits and audience filtering in the nearest service/gateway specs.
